+- **Icon and words wrap together (Eden, 2026-11-12; BUG-94, BUG-95).** At 200% text and narrow widths, an icon never sits alone on a line.
+  - **Nav rows with an icon** (Chat sidebar channels, groups, DMs, Needs you, Mentions, Threads) are laid out as the icon followed by a content column (`flex items-start gap-x-3`; the icon gets `shrink-0`; the column gets `min-w-0 flex-1`).
+    - The label wraps only between words. Never use `break-words` or `overflow-wrap:anywhere` on fixed labels. `overflow-wrap:anywhere` is only for ids, paths (§6) and names people typed.
+    - The count follows the label and wraps below it, aligned to the start.
+    - Chat sidebar nav icons are capped at 32 CSS px (`max-w-[32px] max-h-[32px]`; a rem cap would grow with the text). The app sidebar (§3) is unchanged.
+  - **An inline icon and its word** (a kind badge such as Announcement) form one `inline-flex items-center whitespace-nowrap` unit, and the line around it wraps (`flex flex-wrap gap-x-2 gap-y-1`).
+    - If the unit is still wider than its column on a line of its own, the metadata group (name, kind, time) moves to a full-width row under the avatar. This is decided by the message row's own width, not by a viewport breakpoint. It's a container query local to the message row (MessageRow), with its threshold in em: the avatar, the gap and the kind group's intrinsic width, plus 0.5em. The query is CSS only, and the DOM order stays the same (WCAG 1.3.2). The threshold therefore follows the text size and covers 320 and 960 at 200%. The body stays in its column, and wide rows are unchanged.
+    - Never shrink the text or the icon, and never break the word.
 - **No emoji anywhere** in the UI: labels, buttons, statuses, empty states, notices, sample and mock data, seeded content (PRD §8, E1–E3); pseudo-icons (×, ↳, ›, @, ✓, ★) become Heroicons. **Agent-authored text** (messages, summaries, journal and memory excerpts) is rendered with emoji sequences removed, at render only, never in storage (D7, D19, AC-IA16-1). **Text a person typed** is shown exactly as typed, emoji included.
 
